| Issue Description<br>when using keyboard rule esc:swapescape, the esc key stops working.    Already bisected by Kat in the discord        There are only 'skip'ped commits left to test.     The first bad commit could be any of:     24d433333b5a28f5e484dfdc724262992eb67e91     a3462dd2bd541af6372855917c6ccb5643aeda93     91d15c89bc2f8533d1f852b388c96988368b09e2     b991d36343e19ebff9026c331351b0dbe5b88fc8     ffdf86374a964dba28ca2998e914c0eece13a394     We cannot bisect more!  <br>All of these commits are from [#7320](https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/pull/7320)Expected Behavior<br>esc key (physically the capslock key) should workActual Behavior<br>the key does nothing and shows up in the ghostty inspector as capslockReproduction Steps<br>Set the keyboard rule esc:swapescape (eg in hyprland with the hyprland config, in x11 with xkb, in plasma / gnome with the settingsopen ghosttyopen ghostty inspector (or a terminal application that uses esc, such as vim, or tools with a vim mode)press escGhostty Logs        ghostty      info: ghostty version=1.1.4-6984b1e-nix     info: ghostty build optimize=ReleaseFast     info: runtime=apprt.Runtime.gtk     info: font_backend=font.main.Backend.fontconfig_freetype     info: dependency harfbuzz=10.2.0     info: dependency fontconfig=21600     info: renderer=renderer.OpenGL     info: libxev default backend=io_uring     info(os_locale): setlocale from env result=LC_CTYPE=en_US.UTF-8;LC_NUMERIC=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_TIME=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_COLLATE=en_US.UTF-8;LC_MONETARY=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_MESSAGES=en_US.UTF-8;LC_PAPER=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_NAME=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_ADDRESS=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_TELEPHONE=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_MEASUREMENT=it_IT.UTF-8;LC_IDENTIFICATION=it_IT.UTF-8     info(gtk): GTK version build=4.16.12 runtime=4.16.12     info(gtk): libadwaita version build=1.6.4 runtime=1.6.4     info: reading configuration file path=/home/soliprem/.config/ghostty/config     info(config): default shell source=env value=/run/current-system/sw/bin/nu     warning(gtk): se