#### [pluiedev](/pluiedev) [Aug 3, 2025](#discussioncomment-13976857) Collaborator

| Well part of the reason why it took so long to break the silence is precisely because I don't know if this is intended or not. I'm not responsible for this area in Ghostty and I'm not the one to have made the change to begin with. Per protocol the only person who could really definitely categorize this as an issue is Mitchell. While I don't personally know why he hasn't responded yet (and pinging him doesn't seem to work either), I suspect that it's because this is not a question with such a simple answer as you suggest.<br>It might be easy for you to say that something doesn't work on your system, but it takes exponentially more effort to actually test the whole input subsystem and see what should happen and what shouldn't. Again — we get enough input bugs as-is. Reverting the change might work for you but it might also reintroduce the same bugs we fixed before, and as far as I know nobody really knows *why* that patch works anyways. To me then this is all pending investigation. |
